// Change: new rule
// Title: Application Whitelisting Bypass Via Syssetup.DLL
// Sigma ID: d661eda1-aa47-4a2a-85ff-c39a0515fd5c
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: EinLamYe
// Date: 2026-06-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1127, T1218.011
// Description: Detects execution of "syssetup.dll" via rundll32 calling the "SetupInfObjectInstallAction"
//   export against an INF file. Adversaries abuse this signed library to run local or remote
//   scriptlet/executable payloads referenced from a crafted INF file, bypassing application
//   whitelisting (AWL).
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Libraries/Syssetup/
//   - https://twitter.com/pabraeken/status/994392481927258113
//   - https://github.com/huntresslabs/evading-autoruns
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/c5875f6ddd2f5087d0f0a63a34a2ed4468a9d328/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_rundll32_syssetup_installaction.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "RUNDLL32.EXE") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "syssetup" and ProcessCommandLine contains "SetupInfObjectInstallAction")
